   ],
   "definition_quote": "Given a input tolerance $\\epsilon > 0$, and a (finite) policy space $\\Pi$ ... we wish to solve ... $\\max_{\\pi\\in\\Pi} \\E_{x\\sim D} \\E_{D_b}[r | x,\\pi(x)]$ s.t. $\\E [\\Delta(\\pi(x),\\atrue(x);x)] \\leq \\min_{\\pi' \\in \\Pi} \\E [\\Delta(\\pi'(x),\\atrue(x);x)] + \\epsilon$. Assumption 1: There exists a revealing action $a_0$ such that whenever the learner selects $a_0$ they get to observe $\\bar a(x)$."
